    "title": "Somali Intelligence Kills Senior Al-Shabaab Propaganda Figures in Hirshabelle Raids",
    "original_title": "NISA Kills Al-Shabaab Chiefs, 14 Fighters",
    "slug": "somali-intelligence-kills-senior-al-shabaab-propaganda-figures-in-hirshabelle-raids",
    "summary": "Somalia's National Intelligence and Security Agency (NISA) reported killing two senior Al-Shabaab propaganda officials and 14 other militants in coordinated operations across Hirshabelle State on Sunday.",
    "content": "Somalia's National Intelligence and Security Agency (NISA) announced on Sunday that its forces, in coordination with international partners, carried out targeted operations in the Miirtaqwo area of Middle Shabelle and the Tardo area of Hiiraan. The raids resulted in the deaths of two senior Al-Shabaab propaganda chiefs and 14 additional fighters.\n\nThese operations are part of a broader, ongoing campaign by Somali security forces and allied international units to weaken Al-Shabaab's command structure, particularly its media and propaganda wing. The group has long used sophisticated messaging to recruit and spread its ideology.\n\nThe leadership of Al-Shabaab has been under sustained pressure in recent months. Somali forces, backed by African Union troops and U.S. airstrikes, have intensified ground and aerial operations targeting key figures. The killing of senior propagandists aims to disrupt the group's ability to coordinate attacks and maintain morale.\n\nFor the Somali diaspora, these developments are significant as they represent tangible progress in degrading a group that has caused widespread instability, forcing many to flee. Reduced Al-Shabaab capabilities could create conditions for safer returns and improved governance in liberated areas.\n\nThe Hirshabelle State operations underscore the continued reliance on joint intelligence and precision strikes. While the gains are notable, analysts caution that Al-Shabaab remains resilient, often regrouping in remote zones.\n\nRead the original report from Radio Dalsan here: https://radiodalsan.com/2026/07/26/nisa-kills-al-shabaab-chiefs-14-fighters/?utm_source=rss&#038;utm_medium=rss&#038;utm_campaign=nisa-kills-al-shabaab-chiefs-14-fighters",
