    "summary": "Puntland state has issued a warning to Galmudug administration over plans to arm forces in Galkayo, escalating tensions between the two federal member states.",
    "content": "The government of Puntland has strongly cautioned the neighboring Galmudug administration against allowing weapons intended for the Somali National Army (SNA) to reach local militias in the disputed city of Galkayo. In a press statement from the Puntland presidency, officials expressed concern that arms designated for federal forces could be redirected to groups aligned with Galmudug, potentially destabilizing the region.\n\nGalkayo, a city divided between Puntland and Galmudug, has long been a flashpoint for inter-state tensions. The latest dispute centers on claims that Galmudug authorities are planning to receive a shipment of weapons from the federal government for use by local troops, which Puntland views as a violation of existing security agreements. Puntland has called on the federal government to halt the transfer until a clear framework is established.\n\nThe warning comes amid ongoing efforts to consolidate security forces under the SNA, a key goal of Somalia's federal system. However, distrust between federal member states often hampers cooperation. Puntland has previously resisted federal oversight of its security forces, insisting on maintaining its own military command.\n\nFor the Somali diaspora, this incident underscores the fragility of federal-state relations and the challenges facing Somali unity. Many diaspora members invest in peace-building and economic development in their home regions, but recurring political disputes threaten stability and deter investment. The standoff over Galkayo also highlights how local conflicts can have broader implications for Somalia's governance.\n\nThe situation remains tense, with no immediate resolution in sight. Both sides have called for dialogue, but mutual suspicions persist. Analysts warn that without transparent mechanisms for arms distribution, incidents like this could escalate into wider confrontations.\n\nRead the original report from Horseed Media here: https://horseedmedia.net/puntland-oo-galmudug-uga-digtey-la-soo-mariyo-hub-ay-dfs-ugu-talagashay-ciidamo-ku-sugan-galkacyo/424164/",
